There are plenty of good artifacts for a wizard to wish for, though.
The Eyes, PYEC, and Master Key of Thievery all come to mind; many ilke
the Orb of Fate as well.

With the exception of really good guaranteed artifacts (Magicbane and
Excalibur qualify for sure) I try to avoid creating any artifacts
until I have a chance to wish--that way a randomlly created weapon in
the Castle armory or something silly like that won't preclude me from
getting 1/2 damage+telecontrol, unlimited charging, or whatever else.
But Magicbane'sso nice that it's worth that risk--Sting, not so much.
Orcs aren't particularly dangerous or hard to outrun (or even hard to
kill), so it doesn't really seem to add to my survivability enough to
be worth it.



